### Context Pattern

The component uses two contexts:

1. **ToastContext** (global) - Manages all active toasts, provides `showToast`/`dismissToast`
2. **ToastInternalContext** (per-toast) - Shares `type` and `status` with subcomponents

This allows subcomponents like `StatusBadge` to access the current status without prop drilling.

## Entry Points & Contracts

### `ToastProvider` (required at app root)

```tsx
<ToastProvider
  maxToasts?: number        // default: 3 — toasts kept mounted at once
  defaultDuration?: number  // default: 3000ms
  visibleToasts?: number    // default: 3 — opaque toasts before deeper ones fade
  expandByDefault?: boolean // default: false — start the stack expanded
>
  <App />
</ToastProvider>
```

### `useToast` hook (consumer API)

```tsx
const { showToast, dismissToast, dismissAll, toastCount } = useToast();

// Show a toast
const toastId = showToast({
  type: ToastType,          // 'asset' | 'image' | 'assetGroup' | 'icon' | 'badge'
  status: ToastStatus,      // 'neutral' | 'loader' | 'success' | 'error' | 'disconnect'
  message: string | ReactNode,
  duration?: number,        // override default duration

  // Type-specific (provide one based on type)
  asset?: { logoUrl: string },
  image?: { uri: string },
  assetGroup?: { assets: Array<{ logoUrl: string }> },
  icon?: { name: IconName },
  // 'badge' type requires no extra config — status badge IS the media
});

// Dismiss programmatically
dismissToast(toastId);
dismissAll();
```

### Types

| Type              | Values                                                                                       |
| ----------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `ToastType`       | `'asset'` \| `'image'` \| `'assetGroup'` \| `'icon'` \| `'badge'` \| `'custom'`              |
| `ToastStatus`     | `'neutral'` \| `'loader'` \| `'success'` \| `'error'` \| `'disconnect'`                      |
| `ToastBadgeStatus`| `'success'` \| `'error'` (subset of ToastStatus, used when `type: 'badge'`)                  |
| `ToastVariant`    | `'default'` \| `'inverted'` (surface variant — default is solid carbon050 with a shadow, inverted is solid carbon900) |

## Usage Patterns

### Basic asset toast with success status

```tsx
showToast({
  type: 'asset',
  status: 'success',
  asset: { logoUrl: 'https://cdn.etoro.com/assets/AAPL.png' },
  message: 'Order executed for AAPL at $150.00',
});
```

### Loading state toast

```tsx
const loadingToastId = showToast({
  type: 'asset',
  status: 'loader',
  asset: { logoUrl: 'https://cdn.etoro.com/assets/TSLA.png' },
  message: 'Processing your order...',
  duration: 0, // Don't auto-dismiss
});

// Later, when complete
dismissToast(loadingToastId);
showToast({
  type: 'asset',
  status: 'success',
  asset: { logoUrl: 'https://cdn.etoro.com/assets/TSLA.png' },
  message: 'Order completed!',
});
```

### Asset group toast

```tsx
showToast({
  type: 'assetGroup',
  status: 'success',
  assetGroup: {
    assets: [
      { logoUrl: 'https://cdn.etoro.com/assets/SPOT.png' },
      { logoUrl: 'https://cdn.etoro.com/assets/TSLA.png' },
      { logoUrl: 'https://cdn.etoro.com/assets/GOOG.png' },
    ],
  },
  message: 'Portfolio rebalanced successfully',
});
```

### Icon toast

```tsx
showToast({
  type: 'icon',
  status: 'neutral',
  icon: { name: 'notification' },
  message: 'You have new messages',
});
```

### Badge toast (status as primary media, no icon/asset)

```tsx
showToast({
  type: 'badge',
  status: 'success', // 'success' | 'error' only
  message: 'Phone verified successfully',
});
```

### Custom-media toast (caller owns the media slot)

Use when the standard media types can't express the visual (e.g. a trader
avatar that already carries its own badge). No `StatusBadge` is overlaid —
the caller's `media` node is expected to be self-contained.

```tsx
showToast({
  type: 'custom',
  status: 'neutral',
  media: <EtTraderAvatar avatarUrls={urls} hasVerifiedBadge={badge} piLevel={tier} />,
  // Default surface is solid `carbon050`; use `carbon900` (its inverse) for text.
  message: (
    <EtText variant="body-secondary-regular" style={{ color: colors.carbon900 }}>
      Stop loss updated to <EtText variant="body-secondary-bold">$1,234.56</EtText>
    </EtText>
  ),
  duration: 5000,
});
```

### Inverted-surface toast (high-emphasis events)

The `variant: 'inverted'` flag swaps the standard `carbon050` surface for a
solid `carbon900` card with `carbon050` text (max contrast). Works with any
`type` — pair with `'custom'` for the copy-trading success notification, or
with `'asset'` for a high-emphasis order toast.

```tsx
showToast({
  type: 'custom',
  status: 'neutral',
  variant: 'inverted',
  media: <EtTraderAvatar … />,
  message: 'Stop loss updated to $1,234.56',
});
```

### Rich text message with bold

```tsx
showToast({
  type: 'asset',
  status: 'success',
  asset: { logoUrl: 'https://cdn.etoro.com/assets/AAPL.png' },
  // The default surface is solid `carbon050` (light in light mode, dark in
  // dark mode), so let `EtText` use its theme-aware color — do NOT hardcode a
  // light color like `'white'` or it will be invisible in light mode.
  message: (
    <EtText variant="body-secondary-regular">
      Order Received for buy{' '}
      <EtText variant="body-secondary-bold">AAPL</EtText> at market
    </EtText>
  ),
});
```

## Anti-patterns

### Using toast for complex interactions

```tsx
// BAD - toasts don't support action buttons
showToast({
  type: 'asset',
  status: 'error',
  message: 'Order failed. Retry?', // No way to retry!
});
```

**Fix:** Use a bottom sheet or modal for actions.

### Using toast outside of ToastProvider

```tsx
// BAD - will throw error
function App() {
  const { showToast } = useToast(); // Error!
  return <View />;
}
```

**Fix:** Wrap your app with `<ToastProvider>`.

### Setting duration: 0 without manual dismiss

```tsx
// BAD - toast will never dismiss
showToast({
  type: 'asset',
  status: 'loader',
  message: 'Loading...',
  duration: 0, // Infinite!
});
// Never calls dismissToast()
```

**Fix:** Always store the toast ID and dismiss manually.

