| Status       | Icon             | Badge Color |
| ------------ | ---------------- | ----------- |
| `neutral`    | None             | -           |
| `loader`     | Animated spinner | Gray        |
| `success`    | Checkmark (v)    | Green       |
| `error`      | Error icon       | Red         |
| `disconnect` | Error icon       | Red         |

## Gesture Behavior

- **Swipe down**: Dismiss toast (threshold: 50px)
- **Long press**: Pause auto-dismiss timer
- **Release**: Resume auto-dismiss timer
- **Tap (collapsed pile, 2+ toasts)**: Expand the stack so every toast is readable
- **Tap (expanded, no `onPress`)**: Collapse the stack back into a pile
- **Tap (single toast or expanded with `onPress`)**: Fire `onPress` and dismiss
- **Close X (`closable: true`)**: Dismiss via the toast dismiss pipeline only — never fires `onPress`. Sibling Pressable outside the body Pressable (Banner-like `xmark`). Optional `closeAccessibilityLabel` (default `'Close'`).

While collapsed, only the front toast is interactive — deeper toasts are
`pointerEvents="none"` so taps fall through to the front and expand the pile.

## Timers and the Expanded Stack

Expanding is a read gesture, so it **freezes every toast's auto-dismiss timer**
for as long as the stack stays open. Without this, a pile you tapped to read
would evaporate mid-sentence, since each toast still dies `duration` ms after it
was created.

Collapsing (tap or idle) does **not** resume leftover original duration — the
pile was already read, so each toast gets a fresh
`TOAST_ANIMATION.POST_READ_DISMISS_DURATION` (1s) grace period and then
dismisses. `duration: 0` (manual dismiss) stays infinite.

Because frozen timers can't dismiss anything, the stack collapses itself after
`TOAST_ANIMATION.EXPANDED_IDLE_TIMEOUT` (10s) of no interaction, which starts
that short grace period. Dismissing a toast while expanded counts as
interaction and pushes that deadline back. Swipe-to-dismiss works throughout.

Two things can hold a timer — the hold gesture and an expanded stack — and
`useToastController` OR-s them, so releasing one while the other is still active
does not restart the countdown. `resumeTimer()` is a no-op unless the timer is
actually paused; resuming a running timer would silently extend the toast's
life.

An `expandByDefault` stack is **not** affected: it is permanently spread out, so
pausing there would mean toasts never leave the screen. Only a user-initiated
expand freezes timers.

## Visual Specifications

All spacing values use constants from `core/styles/spacing.ts`:

| Property            | Value                              | Spacing Constant |
| ------------------- | ---------------------------------- | ---------------- |
| Width               | 327px                              | -                |
| Height              | 66px                               | -                |
| Border radius       | 8px                                | X2               |
| Background          | solid `carbon050` (theme-aware)    | -                |
| Shadow              | `0px 4px 16px rgba(0,0,0,0.45)`    | -                |
| Padding horizontal  | 16px                               | X4               |
| Padding vertical    | 12px                               | X3               |
| Content gap         | 16px                               | X4               |
| Media size          | 36px                               | X9               |
| Media border radius | 8px                                | X2               |
| Badge size          | 20px                               | -                |
| Stack gap (expanded)| 8px                                | X2               |
| Collapse peek       | 14px per depth                     | -                |
| Collapse scale step | 0.06 per depth (min 0.85)          | -                |
| Asset group overlap | -24px                              | -X6              |

## Dependencies & Edges

### Internal Dependencies

- `useEtoroTheme` - theme colors
- `EtText` - text rendering
- `EtoroIcon` - icon display
- Icons: `V`, `Error`, `Loader`

### External Dependencies

- `react-native-reanimated` - animations
- `react-native-gesture-handler` - gestures

## Animation Timings

| Animation     | Duration | Easing                               |
| ------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------ |
| Entry         | 300ms    | Spring (damping: 20, stiffness: 300) |
| Exit          | 200ms    | Ease in cubic                        |
| Stack reorder | Spring   | (damping: 25, stiffness: 200)        |

